{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs24 1.0.0 | 04/21/26\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Initial release of {\b EQLogParser-Dalaya}, a fork of {\b EQLogParser} by kauffman12 (v2.3.50), customized for the {\b Dalaya} EverQuest emulation server.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Rewrote {\b damage line parsing} to support Dalaya's log format. Dalaya uses {\b "X has taken N damage from your SpellName"} for player spells and {\b "X has taken N damage from AttackerName by SpellName"} for group/pet spells, which is the reverse of the live EQ format.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Added correct attribution of {\b player DoT and DD spell damage} to the casting player. Previously all spell damage was misattributed to a phantom entity or shown as separate DPS rows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Added support for {\b named pets} (e.g. Bonaparte, Fireballs, Otto). Dalaya logs named pets with a double-space after their name, which is now detected and used to reliably identify them as pets and link them to their owner.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab Fixed {\b pet spell damage} attribution. Spells cast by named pets such as Blood Fountain and Caustic Mist are now correctly shown under the pet owner's DPS rather than as a separate player.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 6.\tx360\tab Fixed {\b other players' spell damage} attribution. Spells cast by group and raid members (e.g. {\b "from Puckin by Ancient: Fatebind"}) are now correctly identified and attributed to the casting player.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 7.\tx360\tab Replaced the {\b spells.txt} database with one generated from Dalaya's {\b spells_us.txt}. This ensures spell names, landing messages, and spell classifications reflect Dalaya's custom spells rather than live EQ spells which share IDs but have different names and effects.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 8.\tx360\tab Fixed the {\b Damaging} field in the spells database so that {\b GetDamagingSpellByName} correctly identifies Dalaya spells, enabling accurate DoT vs DD classification.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 9.\tx360\tab Fixed {\b pet ownership persistence}. The {\b PlayerManager.Save()} method previously excluded named pets with trailing spaces from being written to {\b petmapping.txt} due to a name validation check. Pet-to-owner mappings now survive application restarts.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs20 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 10.\tx360\tab Disabled {\b EMU Parsing mode} requirement for Dalaya. Dalaya uses a newer log format that does not require the legacy EMU parsing toggle, which was causing spell and damage lines to be swapped incorrectly when enabled.\sa180\par}
}